{"qid":"Q128938","names":["Shang Dynasty"],"title":"Shang Dynasty","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Shang dynasty was the first historically documented Chinese royal house, ruling the Yellow River valley from approximately 1600 to 1046 BCE with its final capital at Yin (modern Anyang, Henan), where systematic oracle bone divination documented royal rituals, warfare, and administration. Shang bronze casting reached an apex under late kings such as Wu Ding (c. 1250–1192 BCE), whose consort Fu Hao commanded military campaigns and received her own ceremonial tomb. The dynasty ended when King Zhou (Di Xin) was defeated by Wu of Zhou at the Battle of Muye c. 1046 BCE, an event commemorated in all major Chinese historiographical traditions.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Oracle bone inscriptions from Anyang provide direct textual evidence for Shang rule; territorial extent beyond the core Yellow River region is reconstructed from bronze hoards and archaeological sites and remains subject to revision.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Shang dynasty","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shang_dynasty"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Fu Hao","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fu_Hao"}],"britannica":"topic/Shang-dynasty","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Shang dynasty","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Tang (Cheng Tang)","nativeName":"湯","roman":"Tāng","start":-1600,"end":-1588,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Tai Ding (Wai Bing)","nativeName":"外丙","roman":"Wài Bǐng","start":-1588,"end":-1586,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Zhong Ren","nativeName